01:19:01,104 --> 01:19:05,598
...Longfellow Deeds, has apparently given up his voting rights and left the city.

1236
01:19:06,142 --> 01:19:08,770
the sale's expected to pass with unanimous consent...

1237
01:19:08,878 --> 01:19:12,814
...at the annual stockholders' meeting here in New York tomorrow afternoon.

1238
01:19:13,282 --> 01:19:16,843
Sources indicate that virtually all of Blake's 50,000 employees...

1239
01:19:16,953 --> 01:19:19,387
...are likely to lose their jobs.

1240
01:19:19,489 --> 01:19:21,514
Wait a minute. I'm a Blake employee.

1241
01:19:22,291 --> 01:19:25,021
Holy shit! This sucks.

1242
01:19:26,162 --> 01:19:29,928
Ladies and gentlemen, the bottom line is that this divestiture...

1243
01:19:30,032 --> 01:19:34,992
...will result in every shareholder, all of you and myself included...

1244
01:19:35,438 --> 01:19:38,373
...getting a substantial premium for our shares.

1245
01:19:40,243 --> 01:19:43,838
But before we vote, the company bylaws require me to open the floor...

1246
01:19:43,946 --> 01:19:47,712
...to shareholders for statements either for or against this buyout plan.

1247
01:19:48,151 --> 01:19:50,210
Does anyone wish to make a statement?

1248
01:19:50,720 --> 01:19:54,247
Dismantling this company would be an insult to a great man.

1249
01:19:55,124 --> 01:19:56,148
You scared me.

1250
01:19:56,626 --> 01:20:00,756
It is an unspeakable outrage and it cannot be allowed to happen.

1251
01:20:04,634 --> 01:20:06,795
Excuse me. l got a statement.

1252
01:20:09,605 --> 01:20:11,129
Longfellow Deeds.

1253
01:20:11,240 --> 01:20:14,232
Unfortunately, since you sold me your 300 million shares...

1254
01:20:14,343 --> 01:20:17,744
-...you've no right to speak at this meeting. -Unfortunately for you...

1255
01:20:17,847 --> 01:20:20,543
...l bought one share of Blake Media this morning.

1256
01:20:20,650 --> 01:20:23,380
You told me every stockholder has a say in this company.

1257
01:20:23,786 --> 01:20:25,310
Even the little guy.

1258
01:20:27,690 --> 01:20:32,059
You have two minutes, but remember, I control 49 percent of this company.

1259
01:20:32,161 --> 01:20:35,255
You're gonna have to persuade just about everyone else...

1260
01:20:35,364 --> 01:20:36,831
...to start hating money.

1261
01:20:44,640 --> 01:20:46,801
Hello, everybody. I'm Deeds.

1262
01:20:47,743 --> 01:20:50,803
For a little while, I was a big part of this company.

1263
01:20:51,447 --> 01:20:53,677
I was wicked rich and powerful.

1264
01:20:54,483 --> 01:20:57,179
Now being rich and powerful isn't a bad thing.

1265
01:20:58,354 --> 01:21:02,222
It looks like the Monopoly guy over there is pretty darned psyched about it.

1266
01:21:03,259 --> 01:21:06,251
But the problem is what can happen when you decide...

1267
01:21:06,362 --> 01:21:10,696
...that you would do absolutely anything to become rich and powerful.

1268
01:21:10,800 --> 01:21:13,633
l don't know who licked the red off your lollipop today...

1269
01:21:13,736 --> 01:21:16,034
...but you are preaching to the wrong choir.

1270
01:21:16,405 --> 01:21:18,532
All I'm saying is, when you were kids...

1271
01:21:18,641 --> 01:21:21,804
...did you dream about becoming a savvy investor one day...

1272
01:21:22,111 --> 01:21:24,978
...who would think with his wallet instead of his heart?

1273
01:21:26,182 --> 01:21:27,979
Come on, I know I didn't.

1274
01:21:28,517 --> 01:21:30,212
I wanted to be a fireman.

1275
01:21:31,053 --> 01:21:34,386
I wanted to be the guy everybody called on if they were in trouble.

1276
01:21:34,857 --> 01:21:36,381
I wanted to help people...

1277
01:21:36,492 --> 01:21:39,586
...and yeah, I wanted to slide down those wicked awesome poles.

1278
01:21:41,030 --> 01:21:44,397
But money, that was the last thing I thought about.

1279
01:21:45,401 --> 01:21:48,461
What about you, sir? Did you want to be a fireman?

1280
01:21:48,571 --> 01:21:49,868
No, l did not.

1281
01:21:51,440 --> 01:21:53,670
Truth be told, l wanted to be a veterinarian.

1282
01:21:53,776 --> 01:21:56,210
Cool. Why would you want to do that?

1283
01:21:57,113 --> 01:22:00,014
-l wanted to help sick animals. -And what do you do now?

1284
01:22:00,449 --> 01:22:02,417
l own a chain of slaughterhouses.

1285
01:22:02,885 --> 01:22:05,752
You kind of went the other way on that one, didn't you?

1286
01:22:06,856 --> 01:22:07,686
Okay.

1287
01:22:07,790 --> 01:22:10,350
In the back. Come on. tell me what you wanted to be.

1288
01:22:10,459 --> 01:22:12,654
l wanted to be a magician.

1289
01:22:14,297 --> 01:22:18,324
-And what do you do now? -l operate a pornographic website.

1290
01:22:19,068 --> 01:22:23,095
that makes people happy also, I guess. But kind of in a grosser way.

1291
01:22:24,440 --> 01:22:26,738
-Who else? -l wanted to be a senator.

1292
01:22:27,276 --> 01:22:31,110
-l wanted to be a florist. -lnternational House Pancake.

1293
01:22:31,681 --> 01:22:33,308
l wanted to be a man.

1294
01:22:35,484 --> 01:22:37,315
That explains a lot.

1295
01:22:37,920 --> 01:22:40,115
l wanted to be a Ping-Pong champion.

1296
01:22:42,992 --> 01:22:45,825
But you're not those things you wanted to be, are you?

1297
01:22:46,329 --> 01:22:50,129
Everybody made a compromise, then another compromise, and now...

1298
01:22:50,232 --> 01:22:55,101
...you're about to put 50,000 people out of work, to make a quick buck? Come on.

1299
01:22:55,638 --> 01:22:58,971
I bet if we ran into the 6th-grade versions of ourselves right now...

1300
01:22:59,075 --> 01:23:02,044
...they would kick our asses and put Bubble Yum in our hair...

1301
01:23:02,144 --> 01:23:04,203
...for even thinking about doing this.

1302
01:23:06,449 --> 01:23:09,009
He's right. l would've beat my greedy ass red.

1303
01:23:09,285 --> 01:23:11,617
l would've thrown myself off the merry-go-round.

1304
01:23:11,721 --> 01:23:16,158
l would've tied myself naked to a chair and burned myself with lit cigarettes.

1305
01:23:17,626 --> 01:23:20,527
Did anyone here dream of becoming a psychiatrist?

1306
01:23:20,696 --> 01:23:21,856
Just kidding, pal.

1307
01:23:22,865 --> 01:23:25,629
there's still hope for the kids inside of all of us.

1308
01:23:25,735 --> 01:23:28,169
Please don't break up my uncle's company.

1309
01:23:30,573 --> 01:23:32,200
I always wanted to do that.

1310
01:23:43,052 --> 01:23:44,019
Well...

1311
01:23:45,121 --> 01:23:46,918
...that was very touching, Deeds.

1312
01:23:48,090 --> 01:23:50,285
It appears this divestiture has been defeated.

1313
01:23:50,993 --> 01:23:52,824
Unless I'm forgetting something.

1314
01:23:54,330 --> 01:23:55,922
My 300 million votes...

1315
01:23:56,032 --> 01:23:59,900
...plus the five million votes I control as proxy for the foreign investors.

1316
01:24:00,002 --> 01:24:02,163
So which way should I vote my 51 percent?

1317
01:24:03,873 --> 01:24:05,067
I vote aye.

1318
01:24:05,708 --> 01:24:07,869
305 million times.

1319
01:24:09,178 --> 01:24:13,012
the ayes have it. And Blake Media is no more.

1320
01:24:13,115 --> 01:24:14,878
Not so fast, Chuck.

1321
01:24:16,252 --> 01:24:19,517
Too bad for you, when l was a kid, l wanted to be a good reporter.

1322
01:24:19,622 --> 01:24:22,352
Miss Bennett, I wasn't aware you were a stockholder.

1323
01:24:22,458 --> 01:24:24,585
There's a couple things you're not aware of.

1324
01:24:24,693 --> 01:24:27,184
How to tweeze your eyebrows, for instance.

1325
01:24:27,730 --> 01:24:32,224
Also, when Deeds gave away his fortune, he gave away something that wasn't his.

1326
01:24:33,702 --> 01:24:38,139
-What are you talking about? -l have here the diary of Preston Blake.

1327
01:24:41,043 --> 01:24:42,442
l stole it and read it.

1328
01:24:42,545 --> 01:24:45,810
Please don't be mad at me. l did it for good reasons, l promise.

1329
01:24:46,215 --> 01:24:49,150
I would like to read a passage from Mr. Blake's diary...

1330
01:24:49,452 --> 01:24:51,977
...dated April 12, 1957.

1331
01:24:52,988 --> 01:24:55,252
''I am a volcano of lust.

1332
01:24:55,424 --> 01:24:59,155
''I've gotten this far in business by following my heart.

1333
01:24:59,662 --> 01:25:01,357
''And I must follow it now...

1334
01:25:01,964 --> 01:25:03,226
''...in love.

1335
01:25:05,000 --> 01:25:08,436
''If she just gives me a sign, an opening.''

1336
01:25:08,838 --> 01:25:11,671
Want me to wipe the leaves on your ficus tree, Mr. Blake?

1337
01:25:13,309 --> 01:25:15,004
You can call me Preston.

1338
01:25:17,079 --> 01:25:20,742
Want me to wipe the leaves on your ficus tree, Preston?

1339
01:25:22,485 --> 01:25:23,452
Yes.

1340
01:25:25,621 --> 01:25:26,588
Yes.

1341
01:25:27,523 --> 01:25:28,490
Yes!

1342
01:25:29,725 --> 01:25:31,590
Who was this mystery woman?

1343
01:25:31,861 --> 01:25:36,457
I have here the Blake Media ledger sign-in book from April, 1957.

1344
01:25:37,166 --> 01:25:42,194
On the night of the 12th, there was only one woman working on Blake's floor.

1345
01:25:42,671 --> 01:25:47,108
Sadly, nine months later, she died, giving birth to a son.

1346
01:25:47,710 --> 01:25:49,177
A son born...

1347
01:25:49,478 --> 01:25:52,379
...January 23, 1958.

1348
01:25:53,149 --> 01:25:54,480
That is my birthday.

1349
01:25:54,850 --> 01:25:56,977
to Miss Consuela Lopez.

1350
01:25:57,586 --> 01:25:58,985
That is my mother.

1351
01:25:59,188 --> 01:26:01,884
And the rightful heir to $40 billion!

1352
01:26:02,358 --> 01:26:03,825
That is my money?

1353
01:26:04,059 --> 01:26:06,493
A simple DNA test will show...

1354
01:26:06,662 --> 01:26:10,689
...that Emilio Lopez is the majority stockholder to Blake Media.

1355
01:26:10,966 --> 01:26:13,059
-lt is my money! -That's your money!

1356
01:26:13,269 --> 01:26:14,759
That is my money!

1357
01:26:16,405 --> 01:26:17,770
Way to go, Emilio!

1358
01:26:18,073 --> 01:26:20,439
l will do good things for everyone.

1359
01:26:20,976 --> 01:26:23,171
Free flamenco lessons for all.

1360
01:26:23,312 --> 01:26:25,337
People, people! Please!

1361
01:26:25,548 --> 01:26:29,006
-That is my money. -Don't be misled. These are all lies.

1362
01:26:29,418 --> 01:26:30,680
Mr. Cedar...

1363
01:26:31,520 --> 01:26:32,646
...you are fired.

1364
01:26:33,155 --> 01:26:34,850
You can't fire me!

1365
01:26:35,457 --> 01:26:36,890
l'm in control!

1366
01:26:37,293 --> 01:26:39,022
Get your hands off me! l'm Chuck Cedar!

1367
01:26:39,695 --> 01:26:41,424
At the lake, when you saved my life...

1368
01:26:41,530 --> 01:26:44,158
...which l never got a chance to properly thank you for--

1369
01:26:44,266 --> 01:26:46,757
-You're welcome. -You said you didn't know who l was.

1370
01:26:46,869 --> 01:26:49,337
And it made me realize l don't know who l am.

1371
01:26:49,538 --> 01:26:52,769
So l started working on it and here's what l got so far.

1372
01:26:53,309 --> 01:26:56,745
My name is Babe Bennett. l grew up in Syossett, Long lsland.

1373
01:26:56,912 --> 01:27:00,848
l have brown eyes and l don't know what my natural hair color is anymore.

1374
01:27:01,250 --> 01:27:04,378
When l was in 5th grade, l got a crush on Walter Cronkite.

1375
01:27:04,486 --> 01:27:08,047
And l really did have that Holly Hobby notebook l was telling you about.

1376
01:27:08,190 --> 01:27:12,217
l love Bruce Springsteen, Almond Roca and Abbott and Costello movies.

1377
01:27:12,494 --> 01:27:14,519
l don't like licorice or my ankles.

1378
01:27:15,130 --> 01:27:18,258
More importantly, l know that l messed up real bad.

1379
01:27:18,467 --> 01:27:21,129
And l'd be willing to spend the rest of my life...

1380
01:27:21,537 --> 01:27:23,801
...begging you to give me another chance...

1381
01:27:24,006 --> 01:27:26,270
...because l am so deeply in love with you...

1382
01:27:27,409 --> 01:27:30,810
...and l know it's definitely that forever kind of love--

1383
01:27:30,913 --> 01:27:32,210
You're crazy.

1384
01:27:34,683 --> 01:27:36,150
You have beautiful ankles.

1385
01:27:46,729 --> 01:27:48,162
Let's go home.

1386
01:27:50,666 --> 01:27:53,362
You're fired! You! You!

1387
01:27:53,702 --> 01:27:56,170
Oh, you, sir. You are definitely fired.

1388
01:27:56,839 --> 01:28:01,776
l'd like to stay. l think l can really do some good if l just got another chance.

1389
01:28:05,514 --> 01:28:09,507
Not fired. But tomorrow morning, you let me change your socks.

1390
01:28:11,186 --> 01:28:12,153
Okay.

1391
01:28:13,489 --> 01:28:16,549
And you, Long-Long-Longfellow...

1392
01:28:16,959 --> 01:28:20,224
...you are the one who made all this possible...

1393
01:28:20,329 --> 01:28:23,298
...with your beautiful words and your beautiful spirit.

1394
01:28:23,666 --> 01:28:26,430
And Miss Bennett, with her beautiful research.

1395
01:28:27,002 --> 01:28:28,401
How can I thank you?

1396
01:28:28,837 --> 01:28:31,965
All l want is your friendship, Emilio. You're a good man.

1397
01:28:33,242 --> 01:28:34,402
l'll miss you.

1398
01:28:35,878 --> 01:28:36,845
Deeds!

1399
01:28:38,180 --> 01:28:40,978
-How about $1 billion? -All right.

1400
01:28:41,550 --> 01:28:42,414
Done.

1401
01:28:55,331 --> 01:28:56,355
Holy Jeez!

1402
01:28:57,199 --> 01:28:58,632
l can't believe it!

1403
01:28:59,234 --> 01:29:01,600
-What's that? -A letter from Hallmark.

1404
01:29:01,704 --> 01:29:04,172
They're actually going to buy one of my cards.

1405
01:29:04,306 --> 01:29:08,333
-My gosh! Which one? -The one l wrote for you, remember it?

1406
01:29:09,011 --> 01:29:10,376
Do l remember?

1407
01:29:11,080 --> 01:29:13,913
''Hard to breathe, feels like floating

1408
01:29:14,450 --> 01:29:17,010
''So full of love my heart's exploding

1409
01:29:17,319 --> 01:29:20,311
''Mouth is dry, hands are shaking

1410
01:29:20,756 --> 01:29:23,020
''My heart is yours for the taking

1411
01:29:23,525 --> 01:29:25,789
''Acting weird, not myself

1412
01:29:26,295 --> 01:29:28,855
''Dancing around like the Keebler elf

1413
01:29:29,198 --> 01:29:32,224
''Finally time for this poor schlub

1414
01:29:33,802 --> 01:29:36,896
''to know how it feels to fall in lub''

1415
01:29:37,539 --> 01:29:38,801
l'm so proud of you!

1416
01:29:44,913 --> 01:29:47,643
Can you believe Deeds bought us all these?

1417
01:29:52,254 --> 01:29:54,051
Damn, these things are fast!

1418
01:29:58,460 --> 01:29:59,722
l'm okay!

1419
01:30:00,796 --> 01:30:01,660
l'm okay!

